  "changeMotivation": "The original implementation inconsistently handled results from proxied MCP tools by wrapping every output in a single `TextContent` object, regardless of whether the output was actually structured JSON representing complex MCP content types (like images or resources). This caused data loss and prevented proper rendering of non-textual tool results. The change ensures that if a tool returns a JSON array of valid MCP content items, those items are correctly reconstructed as typed MCP objects rather than being treated as raw plain text."
